    <statement><p>Find the derivative of the function <m>q(r)</m>, below.  It may be to your
advantage to simplify  first.</p>
<p><me>\displaystyle q(r)={8 r\over 9 r + 6}</me></p>
<p><m>q'(r) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{8\mathopen{}\left(9r+6\right)-8\cdot 9r}{\left(9r+6\right)^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p><me>q'(r) = \frac{8 (9 r + 6) - 72 r}{(9 r + 6)^2} 
         = \frac{48}{(9 r + 6)^2}.</me></p>
</solution>
